# {{ title }}

This is a root skill set.

Use this skill set only for: {{ scope }}.

Do not use it for: {{ exclusions }}.

Process:
1. Classify the task as atom, molecule, or compound.
2. From the repository root, run the router with the request passed as a safe argv argument, not by interpolating raw user text into shell syntax. Prefer an argv-safe invocation of `python3 Infrastructure/scripts/lifecycle-and-sync/route_skillset.py --skill-set "{{ skill_set_name }}" --task <request> --json`, or store the request in a temporary JSON/task file and pass that path when the request contains quotes, shell metacharacters, code, logs, or secrets.
3. Load only the selected canonical `source_path`.
4. Follow that module's contract.
5. Record a minimal run observation when telemetry is enabled: selected module id, routing status, and non-sensitive outcome only. Do not record request text, file contents, credentials, tokens, personal data, incident details, exploit payloads, logs, or operational secrets.

If routing cannot run or returns no selected module, report the blocker instead of guessing. Do not enumerate child skills or load unrelated skill sets.
